{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1275423-time-stop","id":1275423,"title":"Time Stop","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2018-12-19T19:03:40-08:00","id":1275423,"title":"Time Stop","content":"A Time Stop spell would require Time 3,4 or 5? The chart presented in M20 doesn't include stopping time. Also, it is not possible to stop everything around the mage? Looks like a 25'x25' area would require 8 successes, is that right?<br /> <br /> If I got it right, there is no way a time stop spell can be casted in combat by anyone lower than a master. How much successes, and dots in Time, would a D&amp;D-like Time Stop spell cost?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3153-lord-revan","name":"Lord Revan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3153_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-19T20:09:43-08:00","id":1275430,"title":"","content":"I have similar question . Which low level (3-) Canon ( or fan-made ) Rotes or Effects can make a mage add his mental actions ? I remember Time 3 in M20 can't really do this ... <br /> <br /> I want to cast multiple spells ...If I also need Adept or above ...To be honest this demand is a little high .","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24560,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24560-rock113","user":"Rock113","date":". 12-20-2018, 02:53 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24560-rock113","name":"Rock113","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24560_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-20T07:03:59-08:00","id":1275495,"title":"","content":"It's Time 5. You step outside the flow of time so you're not stopping time for anyone else. Just stepping outside it.<br /> <br /> You can't use other magic while outside times flow. But you can physically attack people.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11744-enginseer-42","name":"Enginseer-42","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"774"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-20T07:40:42-08:00","id":1275509,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rock113</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1275423-time-stop?p=1275430#post1275430\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I have similar question . Which low level (3-) Canon ( or fan-made ) Rotes or Effects can make a mage add his mental actions ? I remember Time 3 in M20 can't really do this ...</div> </div> </div> </div>Where does M20 say this?. It's my understanding that you can totally get extra mental actions trough Time 3 - you just need to frame it properly, for instance if you want to talk super fast with someone you need to acelerate the other person too or she won't undestand a word of what you're saying..<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I want to cast multiple spells ...If I also need Adept or above ...To be honest this demand is a little high . </div> </div> </div>Perhaps your confusion it's that you think spells are &quot;mental actions&quot;. They are most certainly not. Arete rolls aren't &quot;mental actions&quot; (in the sense Disciplines understands them). You don't cast spells with your mind but with your Avatar, and thus these are &quot;Avatar actions&quot;. Avatars move at their own pace and this can't be multiplied by Time 3 asceleration.<br /> <br /> Casting multiple spells in a single turn ain't easy, if even possible<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lord Revan</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">A Time Stop spell would require Time 3,4 or 5? The chart presented in M20 doesn't include stopping time.</div> </div> </div> </div>Time 3 to slow time.<br /> <br /> Time 4 to stop (freeze) time in an area.<br /> <br /> Time 5 to move outside the time stream becoming &quot;immune to time&quot;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lord Revan</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, it is not possible to stop everything around the mage? Looks like a 25'x25' area would require 8 successes, is that right?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes and no. The table does say that (and remember that you need to add a Duration), but there are fundamental differences between stoping time with time 4 and moving outside of time with Time 5 that you need to ponder.<br /> <br /> Let's see what HDYDT has to say about these effects:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HDYDT; Freeze Time</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">With Time 4 alone, the mage could freeze a single moment of time \u2013 a falling glass, gunshot, car crash, etc. \u2013 for several turns, as described above. If an outside party (that is, someone other than the mage who cast the spell) interacts with the subject of that \u201cmoment,\u201d then it ends immediately. Once the Effect\u2019s Duration expires, the participants in that moment continue on whatever path they\u2019d been headed when they were frozen. If the mage acts to change their trajectories \u2013 hauling one car\u2019s steering wheel hard to the right, for example \u2013 then they follow the new path of action.<br /> <br /> The base number of successes required to successfully perform that action depends upon the size of the action frozen, as determined by the Feats of Time Magick chart; suspending a falling teacup would be a Simple feat (one success), while freezing an impending trainwreck would be Mighty (five to 10 successes) or even Outlandish (more than 10 successes).</div> </div> </div> </div>If you freeze time with Time 4 you don't get to be &quot;spared&quot; of the effects, you get frozen too. Presumably adding Life 3 or perhaps Correspondence 4 to Time 4 you could move within a bubble of frozen time without being affected by it (and without breaking it), but this is the hard way to stop time.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HDYDT; Sidestepping Time</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Using Time 5, the Time Master can step laterally outside the timestream, essentially immunizing herself to any external phenomenon. Things going on inside of her (poison, disease, injury, etc.) continue to occur at their usual rate, but the world outside her touch does not affect her unless she chooses to interact with it\u2026 and even then, it doesn\u2019t experience the effects of her touch until the Effect\u2019s duration ends. Lee Ann, for example, could walk up to someone, punch him in the gut, and walk away; her victim, meanwhile, feels a sudden blow to the gut, but never sees Lee Ann coming or going.</div> </div> </div> </div>Now, that sounds more like D&amp;D Time Stop, doesn't it?<br /> <br /> With Time 5 you can get &quot;outside of time&quot;, so to speak. By getting out of the time stream you effectively &quot;stop time&quot; in all the universe, except you're not really stoping time but rather acting out of synch with the universe. The spell affects yourself and the people you chose (by expending aditional successes), not all the universe, but it &quot;seems&quot; like time has stop for everyone else and it's a &quot;Time Stop&quot; in all but name.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lord Revan</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">If I got it right, there is no way a time stop spell can be casted in combat by anyone lower than a master. How much successes, and dots in Time, would a D&amp;D-like Time Stop spell cost?</div> </div> </div> </div>Since the closest to D&amp;D &quot;Time Stop&quot; it's Time 5 &quot;sidestepping time&quot;, that's 3 successes as per the &quot;Feats of Time Magick Table&quot;. That's it, it's quite easy (for a Master).<br /> <br /> However:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HDYDT; Sidestepping Time</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">As a rule, you can sidestep time only on a turn-by-turn basis. Long-term time-travel is handled below. For an additional two successes and an additional Paradox point per person, the Master can bring another character along with her. Mages in \u201csidestep mode\u201d cannot use magick. Although the characters may affect anything they physically touch, the powers of the universe move at their own speed, not at the speed of a mage outside of time.<br /> <br /> <b>Mages in \u201csidestep mode\u201d cannot use magick.</b> Although the characters may affect anything they physically touch,<b> the powers of the universe move at their own speed, not at the speed of a mage outside of time.</b></div> </div> </div> </div>Note that the mage that &quot;Stops Time&quot; in this fashion can't cast any spell while the time holds still. Again, the Avatar moves at it's own pace.<br /> <br /> \u200bThis is a harder version of a previous rule. Previous rules stated than the mage casting the effect can't use magick, but nothing said that other mages were equally impaired (and thus sidesteping time with a Wonder allowed to also sidestep the iron-clad rule against casting more than one spell per turn, because *you* weren't the one who casted the spell). HDYDT does imply that you can't cast as long as you're sidesteping time regardles on who casted the spell. One could even argue that you can't use a Wonder either, depending if you think a Wonder activation counts as &quot;an use of magick&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","user":"Aleph","date":". 12-20-2018, 11:00 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-20T08:39:36-08:00","id":1275522,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar1683_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1683\" data-vbnamecard=\"1683\">Aleph</a> excellent explanation!<br /> Then it looks like there are only 2 options: Time 4 and a shitload of successes (10+ so you can stop a large area) or Time 5 and not being able to cast spells.<br /> The first can't be used in combat, the other can..<br /> <br /> Either aren't like the D&amp;D spell, so i think it is out of question.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3153-lord-revan","name":"Lord Revan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3153_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-20T12:07:38-08:00","id":1275590,"title":"","content":"Well...since Time 4 also allow to prepare spells in advance to be released with a trigger, you could try to use option 1 in combat by preparing it beforehand (altrough you need to find a way of not being affected by the area of effect).<br /> <br /> It wouldn't be much worse than preparing a spell slot trough a Long Rest...except that the ritual probably ain't going to be much of a rest, and it may take longer than 8 hours depending on the mage's power. Also it counts against the number of spells you have to concentrate upon, unless you lock it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","user":"Aleph","date":". 12-20-2018, 03:10 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-03T13:52:11-08:00","id":1278404,"title":"","content":"I'm wondering how other spheres could simulate the effect of time stop.<br /> Mind could make everybody still, just like Charles Xavier from X-men movies do. <br /> Maybe Life could do it too, paralyzing just like a frightened goat do when in face of danger.<br /> <br /> Although both effects wouldn't stop objects and energies, just living beings..<br /> <br /> It could definitely be made with Forces, stopping motion of everything.Not in an atomic scale stopping molecular vibrations, that would require Forces 5. Just movement of large (visible) bodies.<br /> <br /> I wonder how much successes and sphere dots would be necessary for each of them...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3153-lord-revan","name":"Lord Revan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3153_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-05T04:08:49-08:00","id":1278802,"title":"","content":"Mind 4 to command motionlessness<br /> Life 4 to stop the body from moving<br /> Forces 4 to inverse half of the kinetic energy, thus canceling the other half.<br /> Prime 4 to destroy every kinetic Forces pattern (maybe Forces 1+ is necessary)<br /> Entropy 5 (with Mind 1 or 2) to destroy thoughts involving movement.<br /> Matter 4 to encase in solidified air<br /> Spirit 4 to let a spirit do the trick <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>So, this Zen Master walks up to a hot dog stand and says: &quot;Make me one with everything!&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12022-nonsense","name":"Nonsense","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12022_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"815"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-05T16:42:56-08:00","id":1278891,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nonsense</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1275423-time-stop?p=1278802#post1278802\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Mind 4 to command motionlessness<br /> Life 4 to stop the body from moving<br /> Forces 4 to inverse half of the kinetic energy, thus canceling the other half.<br /> Prime 4 to destroy every kinetic Forces pattern (maybe Forces 1+ is necessary)<br /> Entropy 5 (with Mind 1 or 2) to destroy thoughts involving movement.<br /> Matter 4 to encase in solidified air<br /> Spirit 4 to let a spirit do the trick <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>I can see Mind 4 doing that, since complete control demand this level.<br /> But Life 3 ia enough to control body functions and Forces 2 is enough to control movement (flight by changing gravity/inersia requires Forces 2).<br /> Didn't know Prime could do that. <br /> Matter 3 already can change state of matter, so gas into solido would require this level.<br /> Agree on Spirit and Entropy.<br /> <br /> I guess that the required successes would depend on the shpere used and how it's done. I can see Forces 2 stopping everything in 1m ( ~3feet) per success","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3153-lord-revan","name":"Lord Revan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3153_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-06T04:27:34-08:00","id":1278942,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lord Revan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1275423-time-stop?p=1278891#post1278891\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I can see Mind 4 doing that, since complete control demand this level.<br /> But Life 3 ia enough to control body functions and Forces 2 is enough to control movement (flight by changing gravity/inersia requires Forces 2).<br /> Didn't know Prime could do that. <br /> Matter 3 already can change state of matter, so gas into solido would require this level.<br /> Agree on Spirit and Entropy.<br /> <br /> Since<br /> Prime can obliterate Patterns into quint it is only a matter of targeting.<br /> I guess that the required successes would depend on the shpere used and how it's done. I can see Forces 2 stopping everything in 1m ( ~3feet) per success</div> </div> </div> </div>Forces 2 sounds reasonable to immobilize one person maybe two, but if you go larger than that I would require 4 dots.<br /> You have a point regarding Life..","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>So, this Zen Master walks up to a hot dog stand and says: &quot;Make me one with everything!&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12022-nonsense","name":"Nonsense","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12022_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"815"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-06T05:50:34-08:00","id":1278949,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nonsense</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1275423-time-stop?p=1278942#post1278942\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Forces 2 sounds reasonable to immobilize one person maybe two, but if you go larger than that I would require 4 dots.<br /> You have a point regarding Life..</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, if Forces 2 can do it with 1 people than it can do with more. It would just require more successes. Maybe Forces 4 could do it easier, requiring less successes on Arete.<br /> Also, Forces is the best option, because it could stop everything almost like the Time spell. Objects from moving, energies, even sound or explosions, everything could be stopped. It could even freeze a tv screen with the same image..","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3153-lord-revan","name":"Lord Revan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3153_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-06T06:13:55-08:00","id":1278953,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lord Revan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1275423-time-stop?p=1278949#post1278949\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Well, if Forces 2 can do it with 1 people than it can do with more. It would just require more successes. Maybe Forces 4 could do it easier, requiring less successes on Arete.<br /> Also, Forces is the best option, because it could stop everything almost like the Time spell. Objects from moving, energies, even sound or explosions, everything could be stopped. It could even freeze a tv screen with the same image..</div> </div> </div> </div>At some point minor forces stop being minor and thus fall out of the purview of controlling minor forces (which is the description of Forces 2).<br /> On successes: I would demand 2-3 successes for the effect itself adding 1 success per person or object.<br /> <br /> On the TV screen: it depends on the technology used. Old screens would go black if the ray illuminating the screen is stopped.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>So, this Zen Master walks up to a hot dog stand and says: &quot;Make me one with everything!&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12022-nonsense","name":"Nonsense","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12022_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"815"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-06T12:15:22-08:00","id":1279016,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nonsense</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1275423-time-stop?p=1278953#post1278953\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> At some point minor forces stop being minor and thus fall out of the purview of controlling minor forces (which is the description of Forces 2).<br /> On successes: I would demand 2-3 successes for the effect itself adding 1 success per person or object.<br /> <br /> On the TV screen: it depends on the technology used. Old screens would go black if the ray illuminating the screen is stopped.</div> </div> </div> </div>I just read the Forces description in M20 again and you are right. Forces 2 affects small areas up to 20 feet or less. However, Forces 3 is able to affect &quot;several dozen yards&quot; wich is more than enough for an effect like this. Forces 4 seems to affect up to a mile or more.<br /> <br /> I wish M20 had an area per success table or example tough.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3153-lord-revan","name":"Lord Revan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3153_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-08T12:48:28-07:00","id":1323030,"title":"","content":"I'm resurrecting this thread to ask opinions on how would a Forces effect to &quot;stop time&quot; would work. The objective is stop everything from moving. But not everything like atoms, but everything that we have o our scale. So no need for Forces 5, something with Forces 2 or 3, maybe canceling all kinetic energy around the mage? Could a explosion be stopped (maybe if not in a kinetic energy scientific explanation, but something like stopping Forces to follow their natural flow)? What it would look like?<br /> <br /> To which degrew would you allow things to stop with an effect like that?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3153-lord-revan","name":"Lord Revan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3153_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-08T22:35:07-07:00","id":1323128,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lord Revan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1275423-time-stop?p=1323030#post1323030\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm resurrecting this thread to ask opinions on how would a Forces effect to &quot;stop time&quot; would work. The objective is stop everything from moving. But not everything like atoms, but everything that we have o our scale. So no need for Forces 5, something with Forces 2 or 3, maybe canceling all kinetic energy around the mage? Could a explosion be stopped (maybe if not in a kinetic energy scientific explanation, but something like stopping Forces to follow their natural flow)? What it would look like?<br /> <br /> To which degrew would you allow things to stop with an effect like that?</div> </div> </div> </div>Certainly. Not stopping the movement of atoms is no issue, since that isn't covered by kinetic energy (atomic vibrations are heat. And the consistency of single atoms is the nuclear force. Messing with that would be level 5, and...have nasty results).<br /> <br /> The question is, *how* to treat the kinetic energy in order to stop everything.<br /> * Just eliminating/destroying it outright would require Forces and Prime.<br /> * Storing/absorbing it in something else might require Correspondence in order to transfer it in between.<br /> * Countering the kinetic force to nullify it with an equal opposite kinetic force might again require Forces and Prime - after that's happened you can just take the new kinetic force that's building up due to gravity and just repeatedly turn it into an upward direction in nudges to keep on nullifying it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://is.gd/wodchart\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Probability Chart</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodcalc\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Statistics Calculator</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodarmor\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Armor System</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Damage Roll System</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage2\" target=\"_blank\">My explanation of cWoD Damage Levels</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodstrength\" target=\"_blank\">'Interesting' Strength Attribute Stuff</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodboom\" target=\"_blank\">EXPLOSIVE cWoD STUFF!</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodheresy\" target=\"_blank\">How Technocrats don't think they are Mages</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","name":"Ambrosia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6606_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1567"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-08T22:56:44-07:00","id":1323131,"title":"","content":"Couldn't you just do something like, turning someone's kinetic energy into potential energy, to the extreme? That's just Forces 3 (Kinetic curse lets you turn kinetic ---&gt; Fire)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25315-jihelu","name":"Jihelu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"167"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-09T08:15:58-07:00","id":1323201,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar6606_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"6606\" data-vbnamecard=\"6606\">Ambrosia</a>, first point is correct, completely destroy energy might require Prime. Second one, would only require Correspondence if you want to send it somewhere out od your sensory limits.You could just store it in you talisman, or use it for something else, maybe with outher spheres. It's always good to have energy to spare.<br /> The third, I disagree. To cancel the Forces using opposite forces, Prime isn't necessary. You are just changing its vector direction. This is actually how the levitation rote worked in revised with Forces 2. <br /> <br /> Or you could just transmute the kind of forces from kinetic to potential, like <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25315-jihelu\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"25315\" data-vbnamecard=\"25315\">Jihelu</a> posted. But that leaves two questions <br /> <br /> How would this stop other things, like an explosion or an electrified fence to shock, or even a lightning arc hurles by another mage... I'm beginning to wonder how those would behave in a legit Time 4 &quot;time stop&quot; spell. I mean, if you stop time inside a room with a surveillance camera, would the guard watching the camera live filming see everything stopped? Or a blank TV, since the light is not moving to feed the camers with images?<br /> <br /> And what would be the consequence of having so much potential energy stored this way. How would ot be released and etc.. Of course, canceling the energy instead of turning into another won't have this problem.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3153-lord-revan","name":"Lord Revan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3153_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-09T11:11:07-07:00","id":1323234,"title":"","content":"Time 4 would probably let you stop /everything/ within a certain radius, meaning things get /real/ fucky.<br /> <br /> I'd say you can interact with them with no problem and not have it break (HDYDT says 'anything you interact with in stopped time resumes uwu' yet an EXAMPLE IN M20 mentions a character using the stopped time to go and break some kneecaps with no repercussions and this is a level 4 sphere so hmmmm perhaps it fucking /shouldn't/)<br /> <br /> Stopping individual things inside of a big area might be more complicated, maybe you'd even need the conjunctional sphere just so you /only/ hit a certain thing, but I could see the argument not.<br /> <br /> A room surrounded by people, and you want to stop /on/y the explosion? Time 4/Forces whatever (Maybe only 2). I'd still let someone do it with only time 4 and enough successes probably.<br /> <br /> &quot;And what would be the consequence of having so much potential energy stored this way. How would ot be released and etc.. Of course, canceling the energy instead of turning into another won't have this problem.&quot;<br /> <br /> Obviously you use another Forces 3 to turn it all into an explosion and kill them instantly, but as for regular consequences when it ends...I have no idea. <br /> <br /> <br /> Side note: You could also destroy a force using Entropy 3 if ya wanted. Or Prime 4, and get some quint out of it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25315-jihelu","name":"Jihelu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"167"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-09T18:46:10-07:00","id":1323334,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25315-jihelu\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"25315\" data-vbnamecard=\"25315\">Jihelu</a>, I'm not so much concerned of the spheres and dots to cast the effect, but how to &quot;explain&quot;vit using Forces and what would be the concesequences for such explanation, as well as the difference between being made with Forces and Time. <br /> <br /> I did not mean stopping people or an explosion, bit stopping a whole area where there would be people, an explosion, and even my example of a surveillance camera and another person elsewhere watching the camera filming to understand how it would work. Imagine a room with with a heavy gun fight and then a bomb explodes inside. This room have a camera inside and there is a guard watching from another city. In the moment of the explosion the spell is cast (right before). How would the Forces effect affect everything inside and how wouldba Time do that too? What would be seen by the guard in both cases?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3153-lord-revan","name":"Lord Revan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3153_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-10T04:48:22-07:00","id":1323421,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lord Revan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1275423-time-stop?p=1323201#post1323201\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Second one, would only require Correspondence if you want to send it somewhere out od your sensory limits.You could just store it in you talisman, or use it for something else, maybe with outher spheres.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not quite. You are essentially teleporting the energy into the other object after all, instead of moving it in between, since moving it in between would have...unforseen consequences for anything along the way between the two objects. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> You'd toss whatever you want to actually stop at your talisman. Oops. Hence Correspondence teleporting the energy instead.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lord Revan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1275423-time-stop?p=1323201#post1323201\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The third, I disagree. To cancel the Forces using opposite forces, Prime isn't necessary.</div> </div> </div> </div>It is, since you first need to create the opposing forces. Unless you already have strong enough energies nearby to use for opposing.<br /> Also, just changing the orientation of the kinetic force you want to freeze would not stop it in place - it would toss it into another direction at the same speed/strength.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://is.gd/wodchart\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Probability Chart</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodcalc\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Statistics Calculator</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodarmor\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Armor System</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Damage Roll System</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage2\" target=\"_blank\">My explanation of cWoD Damage Levels</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodstrength\" target=\"_blank\">'Interesting' Strength Attribute Stuff</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodboom\" target=\"_blank\">EXPLOSIVE cWoD STUFF!</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodheresy\" target=\"_blank\">How Technocrats don't think they are Mages</a>","edited":{"userid":6606,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","user":"Ambrosia","date":". 07-10-2019, 07:51 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","name":"Ambrosia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6606_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1567"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-10T11:40:29-07:00","id":1323487,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ambrosia</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1275423-time-stop?p=1323421#post1323421\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not quite. You are essentially teleporting the energy into the other object after all, instead of moving it in between, since moving it in between would have...unforseen consequences for anything along the way between the two objects. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> You'd toss whatever you want to actually stop at your talisman. Oops. Hence Correspondence teleporting the energy instead.</div> </div> </div> </div>Aaah. I see. Teleporting would require Correspondence indeed.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> It is, since you first need to create the opposing forces. Unless you already have strong enough energies nearby to use for opposing.<br /> Also, just changing the orientation of the kinetic force you want to freeze would not stop it in place - it would toss it into another direction at the same speed/strength. </div> </div> </div>That's why you change only half of the energy. This way on half cancels the other original force (now half)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3153-lord-revan","name":"Lord Revan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3153_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-10T13:26:26-07:00","id":1323502,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lord Revan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1275423-time-stop?p=1323487#post1323487\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's why you change only half of the energy. This way on half cancels the other original force (now half)</div> </div> </div> </div>That'd......prrrrooooooooobably not work since that'd be like trying to lower somebody's heat by using the heat to fight itself. Kinetic force in an object won't conflict with itself! It only gets affected by a foreign kinetic force. First law of Thermodynamics n' stuff.<br /> <br /> Although this is such an undescribed edge case when it comes to Magick and affecting kinetic energy, it's pretty much up to various interpretations. Maybe it'd work, maybe not, there's arguments for both.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://is.gd/wodchart\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Probability Chart</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodcalc\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Statistics Calculator</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodarmor\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Armor System</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Damage Roll System</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage2\" target=\"_blank\">My explanation of cWoD Damage Levels</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodstrength\" target=\"_blank\">'Interesting' Strength Attribute Stuff</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodboom\" target=\"_blank\">EXPLOSIVE cWoD STUFF!</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodheresy\" target=\"_blank\">How Technocrats don't think they are Mages</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","name":"Ambrosia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6606_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1567"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-10T17:59:40-07:00","id":1323559,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ambrosia</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1275423-time-stop?p=1323502#post1323502\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That'd......prrrrooooooooobably not work since that'd be like trying to lower somebody's heat by using the heat to fight itself. Kinetic force in an object won't conflict with itself! It only gets affected by a foreign kinetic force. First law of Thermodynamics n' stuff.<br /> <br /> Although this is such an undescribed edge case when it comes to Magick and affecting kinetic energy, it's pretty much up to various interpretations. Maybe it'd work, maybe not, there's arguments for both.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Hm.. The energy is still conserved, it just had half of it directed to the opposite direction, which makes the thing flotaing in the air. THe energy is still there, imagine like instead of one hand pushing a ball upwards, now we have two hands with half the force pushing upwards and downward. And we often see things affecting themselves in physics, think of self inducting eletromagnectic fields..<br /> <br /> But forget all this. You know that laws we are talking about? Those are exactly the ones that the mage will bend to his own desire =).<br /> <br /> Also, what you think about my scenario there with the room and the Time and Forces &quot;Time Stop&quot; spell??","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3153-lord-revan","name":"Lord Revan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3153_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1419"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}